Z||000000||3fifty||06-20-2001||02:32 AM||||I tried to go the easy route. 6x9 enclosures<BR>from Wal-Mart behind the seats (Not). If I<BR>want to change and cut holes in the firewall to recess the 6x9 speakers directly in,how<BR>far from the floorboard, from the sides ect.<BR>do I need to mark my holes? How deep is the hollow? Can't do side posts (no top).<P>Thanks,<BR>3fifty one day!!!!   ||||reg||3
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||06-20-2001||02:45 AM||||The space you seek is not that big, you would end up in the engine bay.<BR>Better off mounting them in the dash, that's been done do a search on the subject.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-20-2001||03:17 AM||||If you remove the carpeting you'll see a seam about 12" up. From that point down and side to side is the area. It is only about 2 1/4" deep. I would not suggest putting a 6X9 there because the mid range and high frequencies won't be heard. Subwoofers are fine because the low frequencies are "omni-directional" and can travel thru the seats. The higher frequencies are directional and cannot.||||reg||1
